       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Maximum dose:** Immediate-release metformin tops out at 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels). The usual maximum single dose is 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into doses (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend. If it is, I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
